### Proposal

#### Please re-state the problem that we are trying to solve in this issue.

New Expensify's Workspace > Overview > Share page doesn't expose the "pre-approve join requests from validated users at your company's domain" setting that Expensify Classic already has. Admins who want this must switch to Classic to view or change it.

#### What is the root cause of that problem?

The Share page (`src/pages/workspace/WorkspaceOverviewSharePage.tsx`) only renders the workspace's QR code and a "Copy URL" action — it has no UI for the domain pre-approval setting, and the `Policy` Onyx type (`src/types/onyx/Policy.ts`) has no field for it at all. The setting already exists and is already enforced server-side (it's what Classic's Domain Admin page reads/writes), but New Expensify has simply never been taught about it — this is a missing feature, not a regression.

This is structurally identical to other simple admin-only boolean policy toggles already shipped in this codebase, e.g. `preventSelfApproval` ("Prevent self-approvals") — a single boolean on `Policy`, updated via a dedicated `API.write` command, with no beta gating.

#### What changes do you think we should make in order to solve the problem?

Add the setting following the exact same shape as the existing `preventSelfApproval` pattern:

**1. `src/types/onyx/Policy.ts`** — add the field:
```diff
         preventPayoutNonReimbursableReports?: boolean;

+        /** Whether workspace join requests from validated users at the admin's email domain are automatically approved, without manual admin review. Mirrors the equivalent domain pre-approval setting in Expensify Classic. */
+        isJoinRequestAutoApproved?: boolean;
+
         autoReportingOffset?: AutoReportingOffset;
```

**2. `src/libs/API/parameters/SetPolicyJoinRequestAutoApproval.ts`** (new file):
```ts
type SetPolicyJoinRequestAutoApprovalParams = {
    policyID: string;
    isJoinRequestAutoApproved: boolean;
};

export default SetPolicyJoinRequestAutoApprovalParams;
```

**3. `src/libs/API/types.ts`** and **`src/libs/API/parameters/index.ts`** — register the new write command and param export, next to `SET_POLICY_PREVENT_SELF_APPROVAL`:
```diff
     SET_POLICY_PREVENT_SELF_APPROVAL: 'SetPolicyPreventSelfApproval',
+    SET_POLICY_JOIN_REQUEST_AUTO_APPROVAL: 'SetPolicyJoinRequestAutoApproval',
```
```diff
     [WRITE_COMMANDS.SET_POLICY_PREVENT_SELF_APPROVAL]: Parameters.SetPolicyPreventSelfApprovalParams;
+    [WRITE_COMMANDS.SET_POLICY_JOIN_REQUEST_AUTO_APPROVAL]: Parameters.SetPolicyJoinRequestAutoApprovalParams;
```

**4. `src/libs/actions/Policy/Policy.ts`** — new action function, copied structurally from `setPolicyPreventSelfApproval` (optimistic update, success clears `pendingFields`, failure rolls back and sets `errorFields`):
```ts
function setPolicyJoinRequestAutoApproval(policyID: string, isJoinRequestAutoApproved: boolean, currentIsJoinRequestAutoApproved: boolean | undefined) {
    if (isJoinRequestAutoApproved === currentIsJoinRequestAutoApproved) {
        return;
    }

    const optimisticData: Array<OnyxUpdate<typeof ONYXKEYS.COLLECTION.POLICY>> = [
        {
            onyxMethod: Onyx.METHOD.MERGE,
            key: `${ONYXKEYS.COLLECTION.POLICY}${policyID}`,
            value: {
                isJoinRequestAutoApproved,
                pendingFields: {isJoinRequestAutoApproved: CONST.RED_BRICK_ROAD_PENDING_ACTION.UPDATE},
            },
        },
    ];

    const successData: Array<OnyxUpdate<typeof ONYXKEYS.COLLECTION.POLICY>> = [
        {
            onyxMethod: Onyx.METHOD.MERGE,
            key: `${ONYXKEYS.COLLECTION.POLICY}${policyID}`,
            value: {pendingFields: {isJoinRequestAutoApproved: null}, errorFields: null},
        },
    ];

    const failureData: Array<OnyxUpdate<typeof ONYXKEYS.COLLECTION.POLICY>> = [
        {
            onyxMethod: Onyx.METHOD.MERGE,
            key: `${ONYXKEYS.COLLECTION.POLICY}${policyID}`,
            value: {
                isJoinRequestAutoApproved: currentIsJoinRequestAutoApproved ?? null,
                pendingFields: {isJoinRequestAutoApproved: null},
                errorFields: {isJoinRequestAutoApproved: ErrorUtils.getMicroSecondOnyxErrorWithTranslationKey('common.genericErrorMessage')},
            },
        },
    ];

    const parameters: SetPolicyJoinRequestAutoApprovalParams = {policyID, isJoinRequestAutoApproved};

    API.write(WRITE_COMMANDS.SET_POLICY_JOIN_REQUEST_AUTO_APPROVAL, parameters, {optimisticData, successData, failureData});
}
```

**5. `src/languages/en.ts`** — new translation (locale files other than `en.ts` are generated, per `contributingGuides/HOW_TO_AUDIT_TRANSLATIONS.md`, and are not hand-edited):
```diff
             shareNote: { ... },
+            joinRequestAutoApproval: {
+                title: (domain: string) => `Pre-approve join requests from ${domain}`,
+            },
```

**6. `src/pages/workspace/WorkspaceOverviewSharePage.tsx`** — render the toggle below "Copy URL", using the shared `ToggleSettingOptionRow` component (the same row component used by every other single-boolean workspace setting in the app, e.g. in `ExpenseReportRulesSection.tsx`):
```diff
                             )}
                         </View>
+                        {canPreApproveJoinRequestsFromDomain && (
+                            <View style={[styles.mt3, styles.ph4]}>
+                                <ToggleSettingOptionRow
+                                    title={translate('workspace.common.joinRequestAutoApproval.title', adminEmailDomain)}
+                                    switchAccessibilityLabel={translate('workspace.common.joinRequestAutoApproval.title', adminEmailDomain)}
+                                    switchSentryLabel={CONST.SENTRY_LABEL.WORKSPACE.OVERVIEW.SHARE_JOIN_REQUEST_AUTO_APPROVAL_SWITCH}
+                                    isActive={!!policy?.isJoinRequestAutoApproved}
+                                    pendingAction={policy?.pendingFields?.isJoinRequestAutoApproved ?? policy?.pendingAction}
+                                    onToggle={(isEnabled) => {
+                                        if (!policyID) {
+                                            return;
+                                        }
+                                        setPolicyJoinRequestAutoApproval(policyID, isEnabled, policy?.isJoinRequestAutoApproved);
+                                    }}
+                                />
+                            </View>
+                        )}
```
`adminEmailDomain` is derived with the existing `getEmailDomain()` helper (`@libs/LoginUtils`), and the toggle is only shown when `!isDomainPublic(adminEmailDomain)` — mirroring Classic's own eligibility rule that this setting only applies to a real company domain, never a public provider like gmail.com.

**Tests added** (`tests/actions/PolicyTest.ts`, following the existing `setPolicyPreventSelfApproval`/`setPolicyPreventPayoutNonReimbursableReports` test blocks):
- Enabling the setting writes the optimistic value and `pendingFields.UPDATE`, then clears `pendingFields` on success.
- A failed request rolls the value back and sets `errorFields`.
- Calling the action with the value unchanged is a no-op (no API call, no pending state).
